      "patternHeading": "What you have been reading",
      "patternText": "John 1:1–19 is the stretch of the Gospel that Lessons I–IX have opened, word by word. You have seen subjects and predicates stay in the nominative after ἦν, ἐστίν, and ἐγένετο; prepositions with a fixed case (πρός and εἰς with the accusative, ἐν with the dative, ἐκ, διά, περί, ἀντί, παρά “from,” and χωρίς with the genitive); ἵνα with the subjunctive; the attributive and predicate positions of the adjective; third-declension genitives; and participles with the article, ὁ ἐρχόμενος, he who comes. Harper’s review asks you to read the Greek of 1:1–19 aloud, to write it from the English, and to sort the forms you have met. Nothing new is being introduced here; the work is to hold on to what you already have.",
