      "patternHeading": "What you have been reading",
      "patternText": "John 1 is now complete. Lessons I–IX opened 1:1–19: the Word, the true light, the Word become flesh, μονογενὴς θεός in 1:18. Lessons XI–XIX have opened 1:20–51 word by word: John’s confession, the voice in the wilderness, the baptism in water, the Lamb of God, the Spirit descending, the first disciples, Cephas, Philip, and Nathanael under the fig tree. You have seen the temporal augment, ὅτι introducing a quotation, crasis and elision, first aorists of vowel and liquid verbs, participles with and without the article, reduplication in the perfect, predicate nouns and adjectives, and the article with attributives and with names.",
