      "patternHeading": "What you have been reading",
      "patternText": "John 5–9 is now a connected stretch. At the pool called Βηθζαθά a man takes up his mat and walks; the Father is still working, and the one who hears and believes has already passed out of death into life. Five thousand are fed; he walks on the sea; he is the bread of life, and Peter says, Lord, to whom shall we go? You have the words of eternal life. At the feast his teaching is not his own; if anyone thirsts, let him come and drink. He is the light of the world; the truth will set you free; before Abraham came to be, I am. A man born blind washes in Siloam and sees; one thing he knows: though he was blind, now he sees. You have now seen the comparative with a genitive or ἤ, clauses with ἄν and the subjunctive, four forms of condition and the contrary-to-fact type in full, the infinitive as object, the dative of time, οὐ μή, οὐ and μή, apposition, the genitive absolute, δέ and ἀλλά, the partitive genitive, a collective subject with a plural predicate, sentence and word questions, and τοιοῦτος with and without the article.",
